; Extension §5: recursion through negation. `p` is defined by the absence of
; `q`, and `q` is defined by `p`, so no stratum order exists and the fixpoint
; would have no least solution. Rejected at read time, at the `(not …)`, naming
; the whole cycle.
;
; The bodies are range-restricted on purpose: this fixture must fail
; stratification and nothing else.

(relation p (person))
(relation q (person))

(rule (p X)
  (is X.reports-to Y)
  (not (q X)))

(rule (q X)
  (p X))
